	"Consumers": [],
	"Description": "Sign-in, session and MFA attacks against Okta users: risky or anomalous sign-ins, sessions from several countries, MFA push bombing, Admin Console access with new behaviors, phishing-resistant authenticator declines, impersonation, third-party IdP failures and unauthorized app access. Usually routed to the SOC / on-call queue.\n\nNo consumers are attached. Next step after install: add a consumer flow to this alert (email, Slack, Teams, webhook, Jira, ...) to route it where your team works. Alert events are also written to the shared _alerts tag (Contents._vendor is Okta), so you can search them without a consumer. Each producer is a scheduled search; disable a producer to turn off one detection without turning off the alert.",
